From 0794942d2bd69ac7423ed9076087ea914b9a610d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:49:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: expose HAS_STATE state roots in Chronik

Chronik's Rust V2 output codec did not know the HAS_STATE flag, so it
rejected or misparsed the outputs that stateful contracts create. The
codec now decodes and encodes the 32-byte state root that follows the
token field. It rejects a zero root, a root on a burn output, and a
root without the flag. Each indexed output also exposes the root:
TxOutput.state_root (proto field 7) in the protobuf API, and has_state
and state_root in the explorer output JSON.

The C++ bridge masks the flags it forwards, then appends the node's
stateRoot so that Rust re-encodes the exact wire bytes. Codec, indexer
and explorer unit tests cover these cases. When Chronik is compiled,
feature_v2_vm_opcodes.py checks both the protobuf and the explorer
output for the vault's state root.

Tier: V2
